 "summary": "A through-hole terminal block on a 2.54 mm pitch whose wires enter from the top, at right angles to the board. Each pole stands on two solder pins, one in each of two rows 5.08 mm apart, so the footprint is a 2 × P grid of 1.20 mm holes. It takes 26 to 20 AWG wire (0.5 mm² solid or flexible) stripped to 11.0 mm and is rated 2 A, 150 V under UL/CUL use group B and 63, 160 or 320 V under IEC depending on overvoltage category and pollution degree. The housing is PA66 to UL94V-0 with tin-plated copper-alloy contacts, for -40 to +105 °C.",
